\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Aerodynamic Load Distribution --- Downforce ($C_l$) and Drag ($C_d$) Contribution by Component, comparing Z-mode (high-downforce cornering) and X-mode (ultra-low-drag straight-line) configurations. Total Z-mode: $C_l = 3.20$, $C_d = 1.00$ ($C_l/C_d = 3.20$). Total X-mode: $C_l = 2.80$, $C_d = 0.65$ ($C_l/C_d = 4.31$). Floor and venturi tunnels constitute the dominant downforce source ($\approx $55\% of total $C_l$), remaining invariant across active aero modes. Active aero achieves 35\% total drag reduction, primarily through rear wing flattening ($-53\%$) and front wing adaptation ($-57\%$). Component coefficients derived from RANS CFD (ANSYS Fluent / OpenFOAM); frontal reference area $A = 1.5$\,m$^2$.}}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:aero_load_distribution}{{2}{11}{Aerodynamic Load Distribution --- Downforce ($C_l$) and Drag ($C_d$) Contribution by Component, comparing Z-mode (high-downforce cornering) and X-mode (ultra-low-drag straight-line) configurations. Total Z-mode: $C_l = 3.20$, $C_d = 1.00$ ($C_l/C_d = 3.20$). Total X-mode: $C_l = 2.80$, $C_d = 0.65$ ($C_l/C_d = 4.31$). Floor and venturi tunnels constitute the dominant downforce source ($\approx $55\% of total $C_l$), remaining invariant across active aero modes. Active aero achieves 35\% total drag reduction, primarily through rear wing flattening ($-53\%$) and front wing adaptation ($-57\%$). Component coefficients derived from RANS CFD (ANSYS Fluent / OpenFOAM); frontal reference area $A = 1.5$\,m$^2$}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:aero_load_distribution@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][10][]11}{}{}{}}
